{
  "anomaly_detected": true,
  "confidence": 0.78,
  "anomalies": [
    {
      "category": "short_to_ground",
      "components": ["J4"],
      "pins": ["J4.1", "J4.2", "J4.3"],
      "nets": ["BAT+", "BAT-", "GND"],
      "observed": "On the EthernetAndPower sheet the barrel jack J4 is wired with pin 1 (center) → global label BAT- and pin 3 → global label BAT+, while pin 2 → GND. The in-sheet note states '2 and 3 are shorted with no plug / 1 is center, center is positive.'",
      "expected": "The specification's reference netlist states 'J4.1→BAT+ (center/positive), J4.2→GND (sleeve), J4.3→BAT-'. The center (positive) pin must be BAT+ and the ring pin must be BAT-, so that the normally-closed 2-3 contact joins GND to BAT- (harmless, since BAT- is the cell negative) and opening it on plug insertion disconnects the battery.",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "J4 (Barrel_Jack_Switch): pin 2 → GND, pin 3 → BAT+, pin 1 → BAT-; note '2 and 3 are shorted with no plug, 1 is center, center is positive' (EthernetAndPower.kicad_sch)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "Netlist: J4.1→BAT+ (center/positive), J4.2→GND (sleeve), J4.3→BAT-. Since pins 2 and 3 are normally shorted (per the note) ... inserting a DC plug breaks that short — disconnecting the battery."}
      ],
      "impact": "The center/ring pins are swapped relative to the intended design. With no DC plug inserted the internal 2-3 contact shorts GND (pin 2) directly to BAT+ (pin 3), dead-shorting the positive rail to ground (the exact 'SHORTS BATTERY!' condition logged in commit a1d9676); with a plug inserted the adapter's positive center pin is driven onto BAT- (reverse polarity to the whole board). Either way the board cannot power up correctly.",
      "confidence": 0.8
    },
    {
      "category": "wrong_value",
      "components": ["C1"],
      "pins": ["C1.1", "C1.2"],
      "nets": ["Display_Power_Switch", "GND"],
      "observed": "On the EPD_Driver sheet C1 (input decoupling cap on the Display_Power_Switch rail to GND) is drawn with value 0.1 µF / 16 V.",
      "expected": "The specification's PDI-matching table assigns schematic C1 to the PDI 'C2 default' group of 1 µF / 25 V ('C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V').",
      "evidence": [
        {"source": "schematic", "quote": "C1 = 0.1uF/16V (EPD_Driver.kicad_sch)"},
        {"source": "spec", "quote": "C2 default: 1 µF/25 V | C1/C5/C7/C8/C9/C10 = 1 µF/25 V | Matches default"}
      ],
      "impact": "The boost-converter input bulk capacitor is 10× smaller (and lower voltage-rated) than the reference value, reducing input decoupling to the EPD charge pump; this is a value/rating deviation from the intended PDI G1 design and can cause input-rail droop during EPD refresh.",
      "confidence": 0.62
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The build deviates from the intended design in two places: the DC barrel jack J4 has its center and ring pins swapped (pin 1→BAT-, pin 3→BAT+) versus the spec's pin 1→BAT+/pin 3→BAT-, which makes the normally-closed jack contact short BAT+ to GND when no plug is inserted; and EPD input capacitor C1 is 0.1 µF/16 V instead of the specified 1 µF/25 V. The J4 swap is the dominant, high-impact anomaly."
}

